WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.220
Sediment on a continental slope becomes unstable and

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.900
fails. The mixture of sediment and water is

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.800
denser than the surrounding seawater, so gravity drives

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.660
it downslope. A turbidity current can erode a

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.300
submarine canyon and carry sediment into deep water.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.520
At the foot of the slope, it spreads,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.980
slows, and deposits a submarine fan. Coarser grains

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.920
settle before finer grains, leaving a graded bed

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.180
that becomes finer upward.
